{"name":"Arizona Tree Frog","hex":"#669264","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tree","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial woody plant taller and larger than a shrub with a wooden trunk and, at some distance from the ground, having leaves and branches.","Any other plant (such as a large shrub or herb) that is reminiscent of the above in form and size."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To chase (an animal or person) up a tree.","To place in a tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree"},{"term":"frog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a class of small tailless amphibians of the order Anura that typically hop.","A member of this class that is not a toad."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt or trap frogs.","To use a pronged plater to transfer (cells) to another plate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arizona tree frog","blocks":[{"text":"These species of tree frogs in the family Hylidae are commonly referred to as the Arizona tree frog:"},{"items":["Canyon tree frog","Mountain tree frog, listed as the official Arizona state amphibian, but as currently circumscribed does not occur in Arizona","Arizona tree frog, previously considered a synonym of Hyla eximia, present in Arizona"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arizona_tree_frog","wikidata":"Q4791457"},{"title":"Tree frog","blocks":[{"text":"A tree frog is any species of frog that spends a major portion of its lifespan in trees, known as an arboreal state. Several lineages of frogs among the Neobatrachia suborder have given rise to treefrogs, although they are not closely related to each other."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Laubfrosch_cropped.jpg/330px-Laubfrosch_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_frog","wikidata":"Q1144302"},{"title":"Arizona","blocks":[{"text":"Arizona is a landlocked state in the Southwestern United States, sharing the Four Corners region with Colorado, New Mexico, and Utah. It also borders Nevada to the northwest and California to the west, and shares an international border with the Mexican states of Sonora and Baja California to the south and southwest. Its capital and largest city is Phoenix, which is the most populous state capital and fifth-most populous city in the United States. Arizona is divided into 15 counties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Flag_of_Arizona.svg/330px-Flag_of_Arizona.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arizona","wikidata":"Q816"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Red-eyed_tree_frog_%28Agalychnis_callidryas%29_Lapa_Rios.jpg/500px-Red-eyed_tree_frog_%28Agalychnis_callidryas%29_Lapa_Rios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Red-eyed_tree_frog_%28Agalychnis_callidryas%29_Lapa_Rios.jpg/1280px-Red-eyed_tree_frog_%28Agalychnis_callidryas%29_Lapa_Rios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn